# Only hand-edited files belong in version control (source, scripts, docs, manuscript).
# Computed outputs and binaries are excluded: they bloat the repo, duplicate across every
# checkout, and change on every rerun anyway. See SKILL.md "Version control".

# Compiled binaries / build products. A hand-written, shipped bin/runall is the exception.
bin/*
!bin/.gitkeep
!bin/runall

# Computational results — regenerated by driver scripts, not hand-edited.
# Ignore the contents of each dated experiment directory, but keep what is hand-written:
# the driver scripts and any figures the lab notebook links to. The notebook itself
# (results/notebook.md) is not matched by the first pattern, so it stays tracked.
results/*/*
!results/*/runall
!results/*/summarize
!results/*/figures/

# Large binary / bioinformatics formats — never version these, wherever they end up
*.h5ad
*.loom
*.rds
*.rda
*.bam
*.bai
*.cram
*.fastq
*.fastq.gz
*.fq.gz
*.pt
*.ckpt
.snakemake/

# Common generated/temp file patterns
*.tmp
*.log
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Large or dynamic raw data: uncomment if this project's data/ shouldn't be tracked at all.
# Each dated directory keeps its README.md (the provenance record); everything else is ignored.
# Small, genuinely static data files are a reasonable exception (see SKILL.md).
# Note the two-level pattern: "data/*" would ignore the dated directories themselves, and git
# cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is ignored.
# data/*/*
# !data/*/README.md
